cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this laboratory, cite it like this."
title: "Razar — Razonamiento Artificial"
abstract: >-
  An organism in C11 with no dependency beyond libm: it eats raw bytes,
  composes the pieces that recur, forgets without deleting, recalls, predicts
  before it reads, grows its own senses, learns rules, and holds a running
  conversation with itself about whether it was right. It is built on one rule
  — never declare what the organism should discover; build the structure under
  which a behaviour can emerge, never the behaviour — and on its companion,
  that every measurement carries its baseline. Its clearest result so far: told
  nothing but five structural properties of negation, measurable against the
  text itself, it read the New Testament with its own pieces and found exactly
  one switch, "no", then kept every place said denied as a closed door and
  asked why this time it went the other way. NO claim is made here about
  understanding, meaning or awareness; what failed is published beside what
  worked.
type: software
